{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 32 — Statistical inference: hypothesis testing, CIs\n","Objectives:\n","- One-sample and two-sample tests (t-test, chi-square).\n","- Confidence intervals.\n","- Practical interpretation and common pitfalls."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n","from scipy import stats\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n","# One-sample t-test: is mean different from 0?\n","x = rng.normal(loc=0.2, scale=1.0, size=200)\n","t, p = stats.ttest_1samp(x, popmean=0.0)\n","t, p\n","# 95% CI for the mean\n","mean = x.mean(); se = x.std(ddof=1)/np.sqrt(len(x))\n","ci = (mean - 1.96*se, mean + 1.96*se); mean, ci\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# Two-sample t-test\n","y = rng.normal(loc=0.0, scale=1.0, size=220)\n","t2, p2 = stats.ttest_ind(x, y, equal_var=False)\n","t2, p2\n","# Chi-square test for independence (contingency table)\n","table = np.array([[30, 20],[15,35]])\n","chi2, pval, dof, exp = stats.chi2_contingency(table)\n","chi2, pval, dof\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) For two groups drawn from Normal(0,1) and Normal(0.3,1), test difference in means.\n","2) Build a contingency table from a categorical dataset (e.g., titanic) and run chi-square.\n","3) Compute 90% and 99% CIs and compare widths."]}]}
